    question: "Do I need a permit for EV charger work in the Olde Town historic district?",
    answer: "All new 240-volt circuits and panel modifications require an electrical permit through the City of Issaquah or Washington State L&I. If your property falls within a designated historic overlay zone, additional design review may apply to exterior-mounted equipment or visible conduit. Our team handles all permit coordination."
  },
  {
    question: "What if my garage has knob-and-tube or cloth-insulated wiring?",
    answer: "Knob-and-tube and cloth-insulated wiring cannot safely support EV charging circuits. We isolate the old wiring, install modern Romex or THHN conductors in proper conduit, and bring the EV circuit up to current NEC standards without requiring a full house rewire."
  },
  {
    question: "How far is your office from Downtown Issaquah?",
