        <h2>Why Downtown Issaquah Homeowners Choose Us</h2>
        <p>
          Working on older homes requires patience, specialized diagnostic skills, and genuine respect for the existing craftsmanship. Here is why Olde Town property owners trust our team:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Historic Home Electrical Expertise:</strong> We understand the wiring methods, panel types, and grounding systems used across every construction era present in Downtown Issaquah, from knob-and-tube through modern Romex.</li>
          <li><strong>Immediate Local Response:</strong> Our office at 612 Jasmine Pl NW sits minutes from the heart of Front Street, enabling rapid on-site response for charging failures and diagnostic calls.</li>
          <li><strong>Permit and Code Mastery:</strong> Every circuit, panel modification, and repair service is permitted through City of Issaquah or WA L&I and inspected per NEC standards.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent Technical Communication:</strong> We explain exactly what your home needs, why it needs it, and what the work involves before starting any project.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Destructive Approaches:</strong> Where possible, we route conduit and conductors through existing pathways, crawlspaces, and attics to minimize wall penetrations in finished historic interiors.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Our Diagnostic and repair Process</h2>
        <p>
          Every Olde Town project follows a structured four-phase approach:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Phone Assessment:</strong> We collect information about your home's age, panel type, charger model, and specific issues to prepare the right equipment and materials for your visit.</li>
          <li><strong>On-Site Infrastructure Survey:</strong> Our electrician inspects the panel, tests circuit integrity, evaluates conductor condition, and maps the optimal route from panel to charger location.</li>
          <li><strong>Code-Compliant Execution:</strong> Whether upgrading a panel, running new conductors, or repairing a damaged circuit, all work meets NEC Article 625 and Washington State L&I standards.</li>
          <li><strong>Live-Load Verification:</strong> We connect your vehicle or diagnostic equipment and confirm charging operates at the designed amperage with stable voltage and proper thermal performance.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Honest Assessments for Every Property</h2>
        <p>
          Downtown Issaquah's housing mix means every project is different. A 1920s craftsman on Andrews Street requires a completely different scope of work than a 2018 townhome on NW Juniper. We provide straightforward assessments based on what your specific property actually needs, not generic one-size-fits-all solutions. Call <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a> to schedule your on-site evaluation.
        </p>
